{:edb/db-before-t 788 :edb/db-after-t 789 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534101 50 #inst "2026-10-06T02:52:40.987Z" 13194139534101 true] [17592186059375 1100 "Find the determinant of the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139534101 false] [17592186059375 1100 "Find the value of $\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}$" 13194139534101 true] [17592186059375 1145 "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(A) &= 0\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{vmatrix}- (-3)\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{vmatrix}+ 6\\begin{vmatrix}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{vmatrix} \\\\[0.6em]\n&= 0(8 + 96) + 3(8 + 48) + 6(-96 + 48) \\\\\n&= 0 + 3 \\cdot 56 + 6 \\cdot (-48) \\\\\n&= 168 - 288 \\\\\n&=-120\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534101 false] [17592186059375 1145 "Using the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}0 & -3 & 6 \\\\ 8 & 8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12 & 1\\end{aligned}| & =0|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -12 & 1\\end{aligned}|-(-3)|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+6|\\begin{aligned}8 & 8 \\\\ -6 & -12\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0(8+96)+3(8+48)+6(-96+48) \\\\  & =0+3\\cdot 56+6\\cdot (-48) \\\\  & =168-288 \\\\  & =-120\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534101 true] [17592186059376 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n- $\\det(A) = 0$\n\n- $A$ is **not** a singular matrix\n\n- $A$ is a singular matrix\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139534101 true] [17592186059376 1100 "Which of the following statements are true regarding the matrix $A$ given below?\n\n1. $\\det(A)=0$.\n2. $A$ is **not** a singular matrix.\n3. $A$ is a singular matrix.\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139534101 false] [17592186059376 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0$.\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(A) &= 1\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{vmatrix}- 2\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{vmatrix}+ 3\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{vmatrix} \\\\[0.6em]\n&= 1(0 - 4) - 2(7 - 3) + 3(4 - 0) \\\\\n&=-4 - 2 \\cdot 4 + 3 \\cdot 4 \\\\\n&=-4 - 8 + 12 \\\\\n&= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular.\n\nTherefore, only statements 1 and 3 are true." 13194139534101 false] [17592186059376 1145 "Remember that a square matrix is singular if its determinant is equal to $0.$\n\nUsing the formula, we take the alternating sum of the entries in the top row of the matrix, multiplied by their respective minors, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 4 & 7\\end{aligned}|-2|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 7\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(0-4)-2(7-3)+3(4-0) \\\\  & =-4-2\\cdot 4+3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =-4-8+12 \\\\  & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $\\det(A)=0$, the matrix is singular. \n\nTherefore, only statements I and III are true." 13194139534101 true] [17592186059377 1100 "Given that $\\det(A)=2$, find the value of the constant $k$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" 13194139534101 false] [17592186059377 1100 "Given that the determinant of  $[\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}]$ is $2,$ find the value of the constant $k.$" 13194139534101 true] [17592186059377 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\det(A) &= 3\\begin{vmatrix}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{vmatrix}- 1\\begin{vmatrix}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{vmatrix}+ 2\\begin{vmatrix}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{vmatrix} \\\\[0.6em]\n&= 3(12 - 10) - 1(3k - 0) + 2(2k - 0) \\\\\n&= 3 \\cdot 2 - 1 \\cdot 3k + 2 \\cdot 2k \\\\\n&= 6 - 3k + 4k \\\\\n&= k + 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2$, we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nk + 6 &= 2 \\\\\nk &= -4\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534101 false] [17592186059377 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 2 \\\\ k & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =3|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{aligned}|-1|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|+2|\\begin{aligned}k & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(12-10)-1(3k-0)+2(2k-0) \\\\  & =3\\cdot 2-1\\cdot 3k+2\\cdot 2k \\\\  & =6-3k+4k \\\\  & =k+6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the determinant of the matrix is $2,$ we have:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k+6 & =2 \\\\ k & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534101 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277567 13194139534101 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277616 13194139534101 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277619 13194139534101 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277622 13194139534101 true] [17592186059772 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277629 13194139534101 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277574 13194139534101 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277581 13194139534101 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277588 13194139534101 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277595 13194139534101 true] [17592186059773 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277636 13194139534101 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277602 13194139534101 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277609 13194139534101 true] [17592186059774 1020 #edb/ref 17592186277625 13194139534101 