 & 5 \\\\ 6 & -1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =1|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}|-(-2)|\\begin{aligned}4 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 2\\end{aligned}|+0|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 6 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(3\\cdot 2-5\\cdot (-1))+2(4\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 6)+0 \\\\  & =1(6+5)+2(8-30) \\\\  & =11+2(-22) \\\\  & =11-44 \\\\  & =-33\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277623 1000 #edb/ref 17592186277624 13194139534101 true] [17592186277623 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534101 true] [17592186277623 1041 "field-1" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277623 1104 #edb/ref 17592186277624 13194139534101 true] [17592186277623 1110 #uuid "5aa8dc84-e4fd-5d51-b298-97c10fc7b514" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277624 1034 "-33" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277624 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534101 true] [17592186277624 1111 #uuid "cc5a18cf-619b-5487-8d6e-7bb9706e4c13" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277625 1017 #edb/ref 17592186277626 13194139534101 true] [17592186277625 1089 "q-280404" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277625 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534101 true] [17592186277625 1100 "Find the possible values of the constant $k$ given that the matrix $[\\begin{aligned}k+1 & 2k & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & k & 1\\end{aligned}]$ is singular.\n\n$k=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277625 1113 #uuid "bb81a2a7-554e-515e-b220-c04ea2819943" 13194139534101 true] [17592186277625 1145 "Let's use our formula to find an expression for the determinant in terms of $k:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det & =|\\begin{aligned}k+1 & 2k & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ -2 & k & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(k+1)|\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}|-2k|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3|\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & k\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(k+1)(5\\cdot 1-0\\cdot k)-2k(0\\cdot 1-0\\cdot -2)+3(0\\cdot k-5\\cdot (-2)) \\\\  & =(k+1)(5)-2k(0)+3(10) \\\\  & =5k+5+30 \\\\  & =5k+35\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the matrix is singular, the determinant is $0,$ and